---
---
<section id="ai" class="section-pad" style="background:var(--bg2);">
  <div class="container">

    <div class="label reveal" style="margin-bottom:12px;">AI Experiments</div>
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:space-between;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:16px;margin-bottom:40px;">
      <h2 class="reveal" style="font-family:var(--font-head);font-size:clamp(24px,3.5vw,40px);font-weight:700;color:var(--text);letter-spacing:-0.8px;margin:0;">
        Pushing beyond Unity
      </h2>
      <p class="reveal" style="font-family:var(--font-body);font-size:14px;color:var(--text-muted);max-width:400px;line-height:1.65;margin:0;">
        Actively exploring how AI tools accelerate game development workflows — from vibe coding to LLM-assisted systems design.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(260px,1fr));gap:16px;">

      <div class="ai-card reveal">
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:16px;">
          <span style="font-size:26px;">🤖</span>
          <span class="tag">Active</span>
        </div>
        <h3 style="font-family:var(--font-head);font-size:17px;font-weight:700;color:var(--text);margin:0 0 10px;">AI-Assisted Game Dev</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-mid);line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 14px;">
          Integrating Claude AI and LLM tools into Unity workflows — generating boilerplate systems, writing ScriptableObject schemas, and accelerating prototyping cycles. Vibe coding applied to real game architecture.
        </p>
        <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px;">
          <span class="tag">Claude AI</span><span class="tag">Vibe Coding</span><span class="tag">Unity</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="ai-card reveal" style="animation-delay:0.08s;">
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:16px;">
          <span style="font-size:26px;">⚡</span>
          <span class="tag">Exploring</span>
        </div>
        <h3 style="font-family:var(--font-head);font-size:17px;font-weight:700;color:var(--text);margin:0 0 10px;">LLM-Driven Procedural Content</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-mid);line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 14px;">
          Experimenting with LLMs for procedural level descriptions, dynamic in-game dialogue, and AI-driven difficulty balancing — connecting language models to Unity's runtime systems.
        </p>
        <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px;">
          <span class="tag">LLM</span><span class="tag">Procedural</span><span class="tag">C#</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="ai-card reveal" style="animation-delay:0.14s;">
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:16px;">
          <span style="font-size:26px;">🛠</span>
          <span class="tag">Ongoing</span>
        </div>
        <h3 style="font-family:var(--font-head);font-size:17px;font-weight:700;color:var(--text);margin:0 0 10px;">AI Tooling for Game Teams</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-mid);line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 14px;">
          Building lightweight internal tools — AI-assisted bug triage, automated QA descriptions from gameplay recordings, and code review helpers — to make small remote teams punch above their weight.
        </p>
        <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px;">
          <span class="tag">AI Tooling</span><span class="tag">Remote Teams</span><span class="tag">Automation</span>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- Note -->
    <div class="reveal" style="margin-top:20px;padding:20px 24px;background:var(--accent-bg);border:1px solid rgba(26,86,219,0.15);border-radius:var(--radius-lg);display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
      <span style="font-size:20px;">💡</span>
      <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-mid);line-height:1.6;margin:0;">
        <strong style="color:var(--text);">Why this matters for your team:</strong>
        A senior developer who stays ahead of AI tooling ships faster, onboards junior devs more effectively, and brings a compounding productivity advantage — not just today's code, but tomorrow's workflow.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
